      "content": "Your observation highlights a genuine frustration among artists and critics regarding a perceived dilution of technical skill, yet science and philosophy distinguish between \"mastery of craft\" and the broader definition of aesthetic excellence which includes the power of ideas. Many prominent works exemplifying this trend resist traditional beauty standards precisely to challenge societal norms, suggesting that the decline in technical virtuosity has sparked a deliberate re-evaluation of what \"good art\" means rather than representing a total failure. Ultimately, while galleries may prioritize installations that demand energy and attention over those that rely on quiet mastery, this shift reflects a cultural evolution where the urgency of political communication is now considered an integral, non-negotiable component of artistic value.",
